3.2. The Thin Lens Model

In this section, we briefly recapitulate path and light tracing and importance sampling with the simple, well-known thin lens model. We use this model as an example to introduce the general notation required for more complex lens systems.
To compute an image with Monte Carlo raytracing, we integrate the measurement contribution f over vertices x on the sensor and a on the aperture, where ω o is the direction of the ray at the outgoing pupil at y (Fig. 4 ). Note that a and y coincide in this case. The measurement contribution [ Vea97 ] is defined as:
